Hi - This is one part missing feature and one part bug. To display the matrix of a quantity of interest, Zelig uses a new method, "simulation matrix". Using your example, to view the Expected Values from "s.out" as a matrix, you could use the following:
  simulation.matrix(s.out, "Expected Values")

There however is a missing feature in that:
  simulation.matrix(s.out, "First Differences")

returns nothing essentially. I'll fix this for a nightly release. The ticket in GitHub is here:
  https://github.com/IQSS/Zelig/issues/44

Thanks!
- Matt

